From 34cf4048cacbff7a87878b3f90a0e2023e43ceb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex17273747576777 <Alex17273747576777@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:57:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] chore(i18n): satisfy spotless so CI can reach the changed
 files

Unrelated to the string fix in the previous commit, and flagged as such.

: i18n:spotlessKotlinCheck has been failing on this file's import order since before this
branch: it fails identically on the run for PR #36 (build.gradle.kts, @@ -1,6 +1,6 @@,
moving ExperimentalKotlinGradlePluginApi above the shinku.buildlogic imports), which was
merged anyway. The violation is in a file this branch did not touch until now.

It matters here because spotlessCheck runs before assembleDevDebug in build_check.yml, so
the build dies on this file and never compiles the four Kotlin files the previous commit
changes - and it never runs :i18n-sy:spotlessXmlCheck on the 16 strings.xml either. In
the failing run only :core-metadata:* spotless tasks completed; 30 tasks ran in total and
none of them touched i18n-sy.

The change is exactly the patch spotless prints in its report: move
'import org.jetbrains.kotlin.gradle.ExperimentalKotlinGradlePluginApi' above
'import shinku.buildlogic.generatedBuildDir'. Nothing else in the file.

Happy to drop this commit and send it as its own PR if you would rather keep the i18n
change to strings only.

Checked every other build.gradle.kts in the repository for the same unsorted-import
condition: this was the only one.
---
 i18n/build.gradle.kts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/i18n/build.gradle.kts b/i18n/build.gradle.kts
index f2e1228..f3aa2af 100644
--- a/i18n/build.gradle.kts
+++ b/i18n/build.gradle.kts
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
+import org.jetbrains.kotlin.gradle.ExperimentalKotlinGradlePluginApi
 import shinku.buildlogic.generatedBuildDir
 import shinku.buildlogic.tasks.getLocalesConfigTask
-import org.jetbrains.kotlin.gradle.ExperimentalKotlinGradlePluginApi
 
 plugins {
     id("shinku.library")
